  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Perfect future",
   "texto": [
    "The future of a perfect verb is formed by combining it with the personal endings of the not past. Although the form is similar to the present, it expresses the future: **сделаю** («I'll do»), **куплю** («I'll buy»), **прочитаю** («I'll read and finish»). It presents future action as a whole with a final point.",
    "The forms maintain personal terminations: **сделаю** (I), **сделаешь** (you)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Imperfect future",
   "texto": [
    "To talk about a future activity without focusing it as a delimited action, **буду** is used conjugated + infinitive: **Я буду читать** («I'll read / I'll be reading»)."
   ]
  },
